# Explorer inspector streaming

Full write-up: [docs/explorer-inspector-streaming.md](../../docs/explorer-inspector-streaming.md).

Clicks must paint **Identity** (id, name, mode) from the in-memory directory **before** RSC. Do not `await` per-entity TfL data in the page before returning the panel.

## Do

- Optimistic select (`useOptimisticLine` / `useOptimisticPoint`), then `router.push`.
- Pass `"use cache"` work as a **Promise** (`detailsPromise`, `cachedArrivalsPromise`).
- `use(promise)` behind `<Suspense>` in the inspector. If `detailsPending` or the promise is for another id, skip `use()` and show a skeleton / identity-only inspector.
- Keep inbound/outbound with the stop sequence (Relationships), not Identity.

## Don’t

- `await getExplorerLineRoute` / arrivals / status in `ExplorerActivePanel` before render.
- Derive the inspector title only from `state.id` (click waits on the full RSC).
- `use()` the seed arrivals promise while a different point is selected.

Canonical: `LineInspector`, `PointInspectorDeferred`, `app/docs/explorer/[[...segments]]/page.tsx`.
